version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-09-27"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of the OES-512 layout: 512 channels as 16 blocks of
  32 (16 × OES-32), each block scored with S = 0.45·Peak + 0.35·RMS +
  0.20·MeanAbs on the absolute residual and latched at τ = 0.50, plus a seed-42
  synthetic benchmark over four Gaussian regimes and a browser avatar. The
  per-block residual contract is defined in oes32-residual (ADR-001). Benchmark
  results are SYNTHETIC; the regimes are far apart, so perfect scores show they
  are easy to separate, not that the method is operational. Operational, field
  and medical performance is UNRUN (not claimed).
keywords:
  - oes512
  - oes32
  - residual
  - weighted latch
  - synthetic benchmark
